      "writtenOn": "2012-02-22T01:18:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "any reason you chose to do this as a function rather than a class (in a similar way to the legacy migration code) ?\n\nI prefer wrapping multi-stage operations like this into a class most of the time, i find a certain amount of shared state makes the operation less scary looking and can help distinguish between setup, utility function and step",
